nswer-field/correct "q-278108/field-4/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-278108/field-4/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278108" :question/id #uuid "77633d5b-6138-5a2c-b4e6-32f0304f94a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-278108" :question/problem "Solve the inequality ${x}^{2}-11\\ge 0$ using the absolute value method.\n\n$x\\in ($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]⋃[$\n{{field-3}}$,$\n{{field-4}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "Bringing the constant term to the right-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-11 & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge 11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the square root of both sides of the inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\ge 11 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{11} \\\\ |x| & \\ge \\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the definition of absolute value, we must have\n\n$$\nx\\le -\\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge \\sqrt{11}.\n$$\n\nTherefore the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\sqrt{11}]\\cup [\\sqrt{11},\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278108/field-1" "q-278108/field-2" "q-278108/field-3" "q-278108/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "63205c8e-0e51-523a-8dee-cba7c680b8f8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278108"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278199/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer/id #uuid "5830a69d-fe8a-5b43-ab85-692d78c1f8d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278199/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d71f6382-3c2a-53f9-bdb3-d6c66141279d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278199/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "eeef6edd-d744-57a9-8487-7b1d